today we're talking about the updated  gta trilogy getting a trailer advanced  wars one plus two getting delayed and  more my name is davonte chisholm and  you're watching gamespot news  so waking up and finally getting to see  the definitive edition of the gta  trilogy is one thing but then realizing  that it's less than a month away from  release is a totally separate thing and  i am shooketh following weeks of rumors  and then an official announcement from  rockstar grant that photo the trilogy  the definitive edition now has a shiny  new trailer to show off its updated  visuals digital versions of the three  game package will be released on  november 11th on ps4 ps5 xbox one xbox  series x and s nintendo switch and pc  through the rockstar games launcher  additionally rockstar confirmed a  standalone version of gta san andreas  the definitive edition is coming to game  pass on november 11th while gta 3 the  definitive edition will be available on  playstation now beginning december 7.  december 7th is also the day that  physical additions for xbox series xns  xbox one nintendo switch and ps4 will be  released however rockstar made no  mention of a physical version for  playstation 5. aside from the games  looking better players can also look  forward to a gta 5 style controller  layout improved gunplay and targeting  controls updated mini maps with enhanced  navigation  the ability to immediately restart a  failed mission and more switch players  can expect gyro aiming and the use of  the touchscreen for camera zooming pans  and menu selections i'm all for enhanced  visuals but honestly they could have  kept it looking the way it did and just  gave me the better controls and i would  have paid 70 bucks just for that let me  know what you thought of the trailer and  and the way it looks it's a little  cartoony i've seen some people on  twitter not really feeling it it's a  little mixed bag but i'm loving it i  can't wait so let me know  and now let's talk about a game that  isn't coming out this year nintendo has  announced that advance wars oneplus 2  reboot camp has been delayed until  spring 2022. the game was originally  scheduled to launch later this year on  december 3rd for nintendo switch but  following the delay it no longer has a  specific release date announcing the  news on twitter nintendo stated quote  the game just needs a little more time  for fine tuning you'll be battling with  andy and friends soon thanks for your  patience  and speaking of games with no solid  release date stardew valley creator eric  concerned ape baron has announced his  next game titled haunted chocolatier in  the game players become the next  chocolatier to take over a local  chocolate factory and store which are  located inside a haunted castle baron  put up a blog post on the haunted  chocolatier website detailing the new  game and said in part quote chocolate  represents that which is delightful the  haunted castle represents the allure of  the unknown the ghosts represent the  imprint of the past all these things are  important  and if that announcement wasn't enough  for you then don't worry there's going  to be a new state of play next week on  october 27th at 2 p.m pacific time 5 pm  eastern this event will be focused on  announcements and updates for  third-party games on ps4 and ps5 the  event will be around 20 minutes and will  show off new looks at previously  announced games and some reveals from  playstation studio partners so what do  you want to see from this state of play  personally i really want to know what's  going on with little devil inside it's  been over a year since we've got any  type of update and like  come on even if it's coming out in like  2023 i just want to know  but okay let's switch gears a little to  a console update the xbox october update  has begin to roll out bringing the 4k  dashboard to all xbox series x consoles  announced on the xbox wire this update  also includes night mode settings for  xbox series x and s and the ability to  quickly change the accessibility options  from the xbox guide  and there you have it so let me know  what you're getting into this weekend  what you're playing etc and go follow me  on twitter at devonta chisholm peace  you
 

